    "field": "Climate change mitigation pathways",
    "problem": "Comprehensive climate change studies have been hindered by the absence of a flexible method to generate multi-gas emissions pathways for user-defined targets, as existing approaches often focus narrowly on CO\u2082 or are too complex to generate a wide range of scenarios for policy analysis.",
    "method": "The paper proposes the 'Equal Quantile Walk' method to generate flexible, multi-gas emissions pathways for specific climate targets by synthesizing new pathways along equal quantiles of emission distributions derived from existing scenarios.",
    "task": "The task is to present a method for generating flexible, multi-gas emissions pathways that are consistent with user-definable climate targets, building upon the range of existing baseline and stabilization scenarios.",
